  "firmwareSourceVersion": "Official binary reports ESP-IDF v6.1-dirty; exact private build revision remains unknown. Public header/LL comparison fixed to fff9895c82d744c7237be8847347bdd1b07c6643.",
  "semantics": {
    "clockReset": "HPCORE0/1_CTRL0 at2058701c/20 reset3/4; CPU/CLIC clocks independently gate execution/interrupts. GLOBAL_RST assertion resets that hart and its CLIC; shared RAM,boot word and cumulative diagnostic counters persist. This bounded active-run reset-domain interpretation follows core-local controls; not a silicon reset/pulse validation.",
    "stall": "PMU207041ec software command0x86 stalls selected hart,0xff releases. ROHP_SYSTEM20586064 reflects those actual latches; no inference that reset/clock gates assert the same status. Unknown command changes and FORCE_NORST reject.",
    "rom": "LP_BOOT_ADDR20700164 is only a word. CPU1 starts real ROM2f800000,mhartid1; ROM main polls address and jalr reaches guest entry. No host writes guest synchronization or result words.",
    "localClic": "Both harts use10800000 per fixed header and ROM. Previous unsupported +64KiB alias removed; hart-local enable/threshold/candidate/acknowledgment. Matrix+800 remains documented.",
    "memory": "Separate hart registers/CLIC/I-cache input+clock+freeze and shared SRAM,MMU,data-cache bus0. Whole-address-space LR/SC reservation set conservatively invalidated by any successful guest store,including same-value/byte/alias stores. Extra failures allowed; no false success after cross-hart write.",
    "scheduler": "Round-robin one interpreted instruction each eligible hart,with round position retained across run budgets. One nominal peripheral/optional RTC quantum per round. Disabled/stalled/WFI hart does not consume guest instructions; both idle stops. Not cycle-accurate parallel arbitration or silicon timing.",
    "diagnostics": "Fault records include actual hart; current PC is selected before possible interrupt vector fetch. Monitor PC/SP/exception history samples only the executing core.",
    "gaps": [
      "CACHE_TRACE_ENA/cache-error setup",
      "full S31 custom ISA",
      "LP-triggered reset-domain reconstruction",
      "physical PMU sleep/stall priorities",
      "DMA/cache-line behavior",
      "Plus EPD/TPS65185/TCA9555/FT6336U/SD board runtime"
    ]
  },
